Dukovo's folders have plain names (ADR 0113): devices are in /devices,
settings in /system/settings, the system's changing data in
/system/state and the running services' in /system/live. /dev, /etc,
/var and /run are links to them, so programs that open the Unix names
still work. paths.h and ctermid give the new names, so that what
programs print and compare names the folders as Dukovo does: a program
that takes _PATH_DEV off the front of ttyname's /devices/pts/0 gets
pts/0. The paths of programs, the shell and the manual pages move with
the folders inside /system, separately. Dukovo only.

